Subject: [PATCH] venus: also take the vtest socket from MESA_VTEST_SOCKET_NAME

The Launcher engine gives a Wine process only the variables it knows (src/wine_environment.rs:
MESA_*, VK_* and the other graphics prefixes, not VTEST_*), so VTEST_SOCKET_NAME never reaches
the game's Venus and vtest_init fails ("ZINK: vkEnumeratePhysicalDevices failed
(VK_ERROR_INITIALIZATION_FAILED)"). When VTEST_SOCKET_NAME
is not set, take MESA_VTEST_SOCKET_NAME, which the engine passes on.

Applied by build-sysdrv.sh to its Venus build of Mesa main (config.sh MESA_COMMIT) only.

---
--- a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_renderer_vtest.c
+++ b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_renderer_vtest.c
@@ -983,6 +983,9 @@ static VkResult
 vtest_init(struct vtest *vtest)
 {
    const char *socket_name = os_get_option("VTEST_SOCKET_NAME");
+   /* PD2 Launcher: the engine passes MESA_* variables to Wine processes, not VTEST_* */
+   if (!socket_name)
+      socket_name = os_get_option("MESA_VTEST_SOCKET_NAME");
 
    util_sparse_array_init(&vtest->shmem_array, sizeof(struct vtest_shmem),
                           1024);
